From 2408ca1dd7bfd444be8c8916796661ead2fe3564 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:06:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Run Trial of the Crusader stage by stage from Barrett
 Ramsey

Every boss on map 649 is a script summon, so the derived roster was empty
and `dc on` refused the map. Barrett Ramsey starts each stage and the
instance script summons him again after every kill and every wipe's
cleanup, so his gossip flag is a live signal that needs no latch.

Five arena objectives hold the raid on a stage point until the script's
own boss slot reads DONE. A conditional driver (hook 67) clicks Barrett
whenever he offers, the raid muster is ready and the last kill is looted,
and pulls an idle faction champion or twin while a stage is in progress
with nothing engaged: they are released aggressive but out of aggro range.
When the Lich King breaks the floor a bot cannot fall, so a descent (hook
68) puts every bot still at arena level on Anub'arak's chamber floor;
Anub'arak is an ordinary boss row. The decisions are pure kernels in
Util/DcTocRaidDecision.h. The Champions' Cache and the heroic Tribute
Chests are looted as encounter chests. DcCapabilities.h advertises the
support to modules that build beside this one.
